{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":66,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.fullCharacterGen_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.fullCharacterGen_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":793,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L793-L817","doc":"**The full general-`σ_i` seminormal character** `2·χ_λ(σ_i) = (2|R_row^i| +\n|S_off^i|)·h`, i.e. `χ_λ(σ_i) = c_λ·h` with `c_λ = |R_row^i| + |S_off^i|/2 ∈ ℤ`,\nfor a self-conjugate shape and any generator `σ_i`. The diagonal counts are\nequal (`card_rowClassGen_eq_colClassGen`); the off-diagonal class is paired by\nthe total swap involution `τ` (`tauGen`), which negates `ρ`. The hypothesis\n`hnd` (`q^{2ρ} ≠ 1` on the off-diagonal class — no box on the diagonal) is passed\nthrough, exactly as in `SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul`. Fully general\nover any `[Field R]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L770-L791","doc":"`τ` is an involution (total: on the off-diagonal class it is the double\nvalue-swap `swapSucc_involutive`; elsewhere it is the identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_maps_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_maps_off","kind":"theorem","line":762,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L762-L768","doc":"`τ` maps the off-diagonal class to itself (the swap keeps `i, i+1` off-diagonal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_tauGen_i1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_tauGen_i1","kind":"theorem","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L756-L760","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_tauGen_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_tauGen_i","kind":"theorem","line":750,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L750-L754","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_of_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen_of_off","kind":"theorem","line":744,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L744-L748","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.tauGen","kind":"def","line":735,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L735-L742","doc":"The **total swap involution** `τ`: the value-swap `i ↔ i+1` on the off-diagonal\nclass, the identity elsewhere. This is the fixed-point-free involution\n`SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul` consumes on `S_off^i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.mem_offClassGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.mem_offClassGen","kind":"theorem","line":729,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L729-L733","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.offClassGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.offClassGen","kind":"def","line":724,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L724-L727","doc":"The off-diagonal class `S_off^i`: `i, i+1` in different rows *and* columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho_swapSuccSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho_swapSuccSYT","kind":"theorem","line":705,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L705-L715","doc":"**The value-swap negates the generator axial distance** `ρ`: it exchanges the\ncells of `i` and `i+1`, and `axialDistance` is antisymmetric. This is the\n`ρ(τ t) = −ρ t` hypothesis of `SeminormalWeight.two_mul_characterSum_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_swapSuccSYT_i1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_swapSuccSYT_i1","kind":"theorem","line":693,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L693-L703","doc":"The value-swap sends the cell of `i+1` to the cell of `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_swapSuccSYT_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_swapSuccSYT_i","kind":"theorem","line":681,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L681-L691","doc":"The value-swap sends the cell of `i` to the cell of `i+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSuccSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSuccSYT","kind":"def","line":668,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L668-L679","doc":"**The value-swap `i ↔ i+1` as a standard tableau** (off-diagonal `i, i+1`). The\nfilling stays bijective: `swapSucc i` permutes the value range `{1,…,|μ|}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSuccSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSuccSsyt","kind":"def","line":632,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L632-L666","doc":"**The value-swap `i ↔ i+1` as a semistandard tableau**, valid when `i, i+1` are\noff-diagonal. Weak rows / strict columns survive the swap because within any\nsingle row (resp. column) at most one of `i, i+1` appears (their cells differ in\nthat coordinate), so the swap never inverts an adjacent comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_bijOn_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_bijOn_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":617,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L617-L630","doc":"`swapSucc i` is a bijection of the value range `{1,…,n}` (it permutes `i, i+1`,\nboth in range). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_lt","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L611-L615","doc":"`swapSucc i` preserves strict order except on the transposed pair: if `a < b`\nand `(a, b) ≠ (i, i+1)`, then `swapSucc i a < swapSucc i b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L607-L609","doc":"`swapSucc i` is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swapSucc","kind":"def","line":604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L604-L605","doc":"The value transposition `i ↔ i+1` on `ℕ` (identity elsewhere). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_rowClassGen_eq_colClassGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_rowClassGen_eq_colClassGen","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L576-L593","doc":"**The general-`σ_i` diagonal class-count identity** `|R_row^i| = |R_col^i|`.\nFor a self-conjugate shape and any generator `σ_i` (`1 ≤ i`, `i+1 ≤ |μ|`), the\nsame-row and same-column classes of the pair `i, i+1` are equinumerous — the\nconjugate transpose is the explicit bijection. This is the `hcard` input to\n`SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul` for a general single generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameColGen_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameColGen_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L564-L574","doc":"`selfTranspose` carries the same-column class of `σ_i` to the same-row class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRowGen_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRowGen_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":551,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L551-L562","doc":"`selfTranspose` carries the same-row class of `σ_i` to the same-column class,\nprovided `i, i+1` are both in the value range (`1 ≤ i`, `i+1 ≤ |μ|`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.colClassGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.colClassGen","kind":"def","line":546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L546-L549","doc":"The same-column class `R_col^i ⊆ SYT(μ)` for generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClassGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClassGen","kind":"def","line":541,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L541-L544","doc":"The same-row class `R_row^i ⊆ SYT(μ)` for generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameColGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameColGen","kind":"def","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L537-L539","doc":"Same-column predicate for the generator pair `(i, i+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRowGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRowGen","kind":"def","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L533-L535","doc":"Same-row predicate for the generator pair `(i, i+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_sigmaOneCharacter_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_sigmaOneCharacter_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L514-L522","doc":"**`2·χ_λ(σ₁) = #SYT(μ)·h`** — the σ₁ seminormal character in closed form with the\nper-shape coefficient made explicit: `c_λ = #SYT(μ)/2`. Combines the character\nfactorisation `2·χ = 2·|R_row|·h` with the count `2·|R_row| = #SYT(μ)`. Fully\ngeneral over any `[Field R]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_card_rowClass_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_card_rowClass_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L501-L512","doc":"**The per-shape count** `2·|R_row| = #SYT(μ)` for a self-conjugate shape with\n`≥ 2` cells (`c_λ = #SYT(μ)/2`): the two σ₁ classes partition `SYT(μ)` and are\nequinumerous (`card_rowClass_eq_colClass`). No enumeration of tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.disjoint_rowClass_colClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.disjoint_rowClass_colClass","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L492-L499","doc":"**`R_row` and `R_col` are disjoint** — no tableau is in both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClass_union_colClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClass_union_colClass","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L482-L490","doc":"**`R_row ∪ R_col = SYT(μ)`** (as `Finset.univ`) — every tableau is in one class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.not_sameRow12_and_sameCol12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.not_sameRow12_and_sameCol12","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L469-L480","doc":"**The σ₁ classes are disjoint**: `1` and `2` cannot share *both* a row and a\ncolumn (they would occupy the same cell, but carry different entries). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12_or_sameCol12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12_or_sameCol12","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L460-L467","doc":"**The σ₁ dichotomy**: for every standard tableau of a `≥ 2`-cell shape, `1` and\n`2` share a row *or* a column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_two_coord_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_two_coord_zero","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L425-L458","doc":"**`cellOf T 2` sits on the corner row or column**: its row *or* column index is\n`0`. If both were `≥ 1`, its up-neighbour and left-neighbour would both carry an\nentry `< 2`, i.e. both `= 1` — two distinct cells with entry `1`, impossible by\ninjectivity of the filling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_one","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L420-L423","doc":"**`cellOf T 1 = (0,0)`** — the entry `1` lives at the corner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.zero_zero_mem_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.zero_zero_mem_cells","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L414-L418","doc":"**`(0,0) ∈ μ`** whenever `μ` has a cell (the diagram is a lower set). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_zero_zero_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_zero_zero_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L400-L412","doc":"**Entry `1` is at the corner**: `T.entry 0 0 = 1`. The corner is `≥ 1` (in the\nvalue range) and `≤` the cell carrying `1` (`entry_le`), so it *is* `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_le","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L385-L398","doc":"**The `(0,0)` corner is minimal**: `T.entry 0 0 ≤ T.entry a b` for every cell\n`(a,b)` — weak rows to `(0,b)` then strict columns down to `(a,b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sigmaOneCharacter_eq_card_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sigmaOneCharacter_eq_card_mul","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L363-L374","doc":"**`χ_λ(σ₁) = |R_row|·h`** (`c_λ = |R_row| ∈ ℤ`) — the proposition's factorisation\nfor `σ₁`, over any field with `2 ≠ 0` (in particular `ℝ`). The remaining step to\nthe tabulated `c_λ ∈ {1, 3, 8, 10}` is the per-shape count `|R_row|` for each\nself-conjugate `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_sigmaOneCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.two_mul_sigmaOneCharacter","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L346-L361","doc":"**`2·χ_λ(σ₁) = 2·|R_row|·h`** — fully general over any `[Field R]`. The σ₁\ncharacter is an integer multiple of `h`; `fullCharacter_two_mul` at `Soff = ∅`\nplus `card_rowClass_eq_colClass`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sigmaOneCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sigmaOneCharacter","kind":"def","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L341-L344","doc":"The **concrete σ₁ seminormal character** on `S^λ`: purely diagonal (the\noff-diagonal class is empty for `σ₁`), `|R_row|·q + |R_col|·(h − q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_rowClass_eq_colClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_rowClass_eq_colClass","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L313-L329","doc":"**The σ₁ class-count identity** `|R_row| = |R_col|`. For a self-conjugate shape\nwith `≥ 2` cells, the same-row and same-column classes of the generator pair\n`1, 2` are equinumerous — `selfTranspose` is the explicit bijection between them\n(row ↔ column swap + involution), fed to `card_row_eq_card_col`. This is the\nconcrete `Finset.card` heart of the σ₁ seminormal character `χ_λ(σ₁) = c_λ·h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameCol12_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameCol12_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L302-L311","doc":"`selfTranspose` carries the same-column class to the same-row class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L289-L300","doc":"`selfTranspose` carries the same-row class to the same-column class: for `≥ 2`\ncells and self-conjugate `μ`, `sameRow12 (selfTranspose h T) ↔ sameCol12 T`\n(`cellOf_selfTranspose` swaps the row/column coordinate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.colClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.colClass","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L285-L287","doc":"The **same-column class** `R_col ⊆ SYT(μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.rowClass","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L281-L283","doc":"The **same-row class** `R_row ⊆ SYT(μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameCol12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameCol12","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L278-L279","doc":"**Same-column class predicate** for the pair `1, 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.sameRow12","kind":"def","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L274-L276","doc":"**Same-row class predicate** for the generator pair `1, 2`: the cells holding\n`1` and `2` share a row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.instFintypeSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.instFintypeSYT","kind":"instance","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L267-L272","doc":"`SYT(μ)` is a `Fintype` (the `encode` injection into a finite function space,\nalready proved injective in `StandardYoungTableau`). Noncomputable — the count is\nwhat matters, not an enumeration algorithm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L254-L262","doc":"**The self-conjugate transpose is a structural involution** on `SYT(μ)`:\n`selfTranspose h (selfTranspose h T) = T` (full equality, not just entry level —\nlifted through the `encode` injection). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.exists_cell_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.exists_cell_entry","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L247-L252","doc":"**Surjectivity of the filling**: every value in `{1,…,|μ|}` is the entry of some\ncell (`bijOn.surjOn`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_selfTranspose","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L219-L236","doc":"**The self-conjugate transpose swaps cells**:\n`cellOf (selfTranspose h T) k = Prod.swap (cellOf T k)`. The cell holding `k` in\n`Tᵀ` is the coordinate swap of the cell holding `k` in `T` — the entry-level\ncoordinate swap (`selfTranspose_entry`) lifted through the pinned inverse\n(`cellOf_eq_of_entry`), the swapped cell staying in `μ` by\n`swap_bijOn_cells` + self-conjugacy. This is the **same-row ↔ same-column\nclass swap** for the generator pair `1, 2`: whichever of `(cellOf T 1),\n(cellOf T 2)` shared a row now shares a column, discharging the\nclass-exchange hypotheses of `card_row_eq_card_col`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_eq_of_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_eq_of_entry","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L209-L217","doc":"**`cellOf` is pinned by any witnessing cell** — the inverse of the filling is\nunique. If `c` is a cell of `μ` carrying entry `k`, then `cellOf T k = c`\n(filling injectivity, `injOn_cells`). This is the uniqueness the choice-based\n`cellOf` needs to compose with a coordinate swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L200-L205","doc":"**`selfTranspose` is an involution** (entry level): applying the self-conjugate\ntranspose twice recovers `T`'s filling. This is the involutivity hypothesis\n`card_row_eq_card_col` needs, in the entry form the class Finsets are cut out by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose_entry","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L193-L198","doc":"The self-conjugate transpose swaps coordinates at the entry level:\n`(selfTranspose h T).entry (i,j) = T.entry (j,i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.selfTranspose","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L184-L191","doc":"**The self-conjugate transpose** — for a **self-conjugate** shape (`μᵀ = μ`), the\nconjugate transpose is an endomorphism `SYT(μ) → SYT(μ)`, obtained by transporting\n`transpose T : SYT(μᵀ)` back across `μᵀ = μ`. This is the `f` that\n`card_row_eq_card_col` consumes: for the generator pair `1, 2` it swaps the\nsame-row and same-column classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.entry_cast","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**Transport preserves the entry map**: casting a standard tableau along a diagram\nequality `μ = ν` leaves each entry value unchanged (the entry map is\n`ℕ → ℕ → ℕ`, independent of the diagram). Proved with fresh `ν` so the transport\n`subst`s cleanly — the self-referential `μᵀ = μ` case is recovered by\ninstantiation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose_transpose_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose_transpose_entry","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L164-L171","doc":"**The double transpose recovers the filling** at the entry level: `Tᵀᵀ` has the\nsame entry map as `T` (`entry (i,j) = T.entry (i,j)`). Definitional — the entry\nof `transpose` is the coordinate-swapped entry of its argument, and swapping\ntwice is the identity. This is the involution-of-transpose statement in the form\nthe character sum consumes (entry-level), independent of the\n`μᵀᵀ = μ` diagram identification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L145-L162","doc":"**The conjugate transpose of a standard tableau** `T ↦ Tᵀ`, as a full\n`StandardYoungTableau μᵀ`. The semistandard content is `transposeSsyt`; the\nbijectivity of the filling is `T`'s own filling bijection **precomposed with the\n`Prod.swap` cell bijection** (`swap_bijOn_cells`), the value range shifted by the\ncardinality identity `|μᵀ| = |μ|` (`transpose_cells_card`).\n\nThis is the concrete construction the σ₁-character closure needs: for a\nself-conjugate `μ` (`μ = μᵀ`) it is an **involution on `SYT(μ)`** that swaps the\nsame-row and same-column classes of the pair `1, 2`, discharging the three\nhypotheses of `card_row_eq_card_col` and hence `|R_row| = |R_col|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose_cells_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transpose_cells_card","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**Transpose preserves the cell count** `|μᵀ| = |μ|`: the cell set is a `Prod.swap`\nreindex of `μ`'s (`Finset.card_map`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swap_bijOn_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.swap_bijOn_cells","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L124-L135","doc":"**`Prod.swap` is a bijection of cell sets** `μᵀ.cells ↔ μ.cells`. The transpose\ncell set is the swap-image of `μ`'s (`mem_transpose_iff`), so swapping coordinates\ncarries one onto the other and is its own inverse (`Prod.swap_swap`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transposeSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.transposeSsyt","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**The conjugate transpose of a standard tableau, as a semistandard tableau of\n`μᵀ`** — the mathematical heart of the row↔column swap: `entry (i,j) := T.entry\n(j,i)`. Weak rows of the transpose come from `T`'s **strict columns**\n(`col_strict`); strict columns come from `T`'s **strict rows** (`row_strict`,\nwhich holds for a *standard* tableau by bijectivity). The residual off-diagram\nzeros transport through `mem_transpose_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.mem_transpose_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.mem_transpose_iff","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L105-L108","doc":"**Cell membership in the transpose**: `(i, j) ∈ μᵀ ↔ (j, i) ∈ μ`. The transpose\ncell set is the `Prod.swap`-image of `μ`'s cells (`YoungDiagram.transpose`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_row_eq_card_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.card_row_eq_card_col","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L70-L101","doc":"**The `|R_row| = |R_col|` structural core (self-conjugacy ⇒ equal counts).**\nGiven a self-inverse map `f` on the standard-tableau index set that carries the\n**same-row** class `Rrow` (`1, 2` in the same row) into the **same-column**\nclass `Rcol` and back, the two classes have equal cardinality. The\n**conjugate transpose** `T ↦ Tᵀ` is exactly such an `f` for a self-conjugate\n`μ` (`μ = μᵀ`): it maps `SYT(μ)` to itself, is an involution, and swaps\nsame-row ↔ same-column for the pair `1, 2`.\n\nThis is the structural half of the σ₁-character closure: with `|Rrow| = |Rcol|`\nthe diagonal contribution `|Rrow|·q + |Rcol|·(−q⁻¹) = |Rrow|·h` is an integer\nmultiple of `h`, feeding `SeminormalWeight.fullCharacter_two_mul` (with the\noff-diagonal class empty for the single generator σ₁). Robust `Finset.image`\nproof — no heavy tableau machinery here; the remaining piece (bean `qou-tqab`)\nis *constructing* the transpose involution on the canonical\n`StandardYoungTableau` and discharging its three hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho_swap","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L61-L68","doc":"The generator axial distance is antisymmetric in the two entries:\n`ρ(i, i+1) = −ρ(i+1, i)` (via `TableauContent.axialDistance_antisymm`) — the\ncell-geometry root of the seminormal ρ ↔ −ρ pairing that makes the reduced-weight\nsum an integer `c_λ` (`SeminormalWeight.two_mul_reducedSum_eq_card`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf_spec","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L52-L59","doc":"When `k` is actually an entry of `T` (some cell of `μ` maps to it), `cellOf T k`\nis a cell of `μ` and carries entry `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.generatorRho","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L46-L50","doc":"**Generator axial distance** `ρ = c(cell of i+1) − c(cell of i)`: the axial\ndistance of the generator pair `(i, i+1)` in `T`, the `ρ` of the seminormal\nweight `a_ρ` that the character sum ranges over (`TableauContent.axialDistance`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalCharacterConnector.cellOf","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SeminormalCharacterConnector.lean#L40-L44","doc":"**The cell holding entry `k`** — the inverse of the bijective filling. For `k`\nin the value range `{1,…,|μ|}` the filling's surjectivity gives a (unique) cell;\noff-range it defaults to `(0,0)`. Noncomputable (choice on surjectivity). ","signatureChunk":0}]}